<title>USA: Progenics IPO postponed indefinitely.</title>
<headline>Progenics IPO postponed indefinitely.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Progenics Pharmaceuticals Inc's planned initial public offering has been postponed indefinitely, lead underwriter Oppenheimer &amp; Co said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company had planned to offer two million shares in range of $7 to $9 each. It had revised the price lower in November from its first estimate of $11 to $13.</p>
<p>The shares were to trade on the Nasdaq under the symbol &quot;PRGN&quot;. The biopharmaceutical company develops products to treat and prevent cancer and viral diseases.</p>
</text>
